From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:11:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] grt: release the router's working state before the final
 parasitics
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After antenna repair nothing in global_route.tcl routes: the final
estimate_parasitics reads only the routes, and write_guides the guides.
global_route -cleanup (bazel-orfs OpenROAD patch 0010) releases the
router's grid, nets and trees there, unless a POST GLOBAL_ROUTE step is
configured, which may route. On XiangShan's XSTile (3.8 M nets) the
stage's peak goes from 108.5 to 104.7 GiB, the resident set drops by
13.4 GiB at the call, and the ODB is byte-identical.

Not upstreamed. Needs OpenROAD's global_route -cleanup; retires at a
bump onto an ORFS and an OpenROAD that have both.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 flow/scripts/global_route.tcl | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/flow/scripts/global_route.tcl b/flow/scripts/global_route.tcl
index 153c1b3..39a52be 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/global_route.tcl
+++ b/flow/scripts/global_route.tcl
@@ -181,6 +181,11 @@ proc global_route_helper { } {
     check_antennas -report_file $::env(REPORTS_DIR)/grt_antennas.log
   }
 
+  # Nothing below routes, unless a POST GLOBAL_ROUTE step does: release the
+  # router's working state before the parasitics, which read only the routes.
+  if { ![env_var_exists_and_non_empty POST_GLOBAL_ROUTE_TCL] } {
+    log_cmd global_route -cleanup
+  }
   puts "Estimate parasitics..."
   log_cmd estimate_parasitics -global_routing
 
